{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-2co-11-1","title":"2 Corinthians 11:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Out of his jealousy over the Corinthians, who seemed to make more account of the false apostles than of him, he enters into a forced commendation of himself, 5 of his equality with the chief apostles, 7 of his preaching the gospel to them freely, and without any charge to them; 13 shewing that he was not inferior to those deceitful workers in any legal prerogative; 23 and in the service of Christ, and in all kinds of sufferings for his ministry, far superior.</p>\n<p>Would. Nu 11:29; Jos 7:7; 2Ki 5:3; Ac 26:29; 1Co 4:8 bear with me a. 4; Ac 18:14; Heb 5:2 in. 16,17,19,21; 5:13; 12:11; 1Co 1:21; 3:18; 4:10 bear with me. or, ye do bear with me.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-2","title":"2 Corinthians 11:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>jealous. Ga 4:11,17-19; Php 1:8; 1Th 2:11 I have. Ge 24:2-5,58-67; Ps 45:10,11; Isa 54:5; 62:4,5; Ho 2:19,20 Joh 3:29; Ro 7:4; 1Co 4:15 I may. Eph 5:27; Col 1:28 a chaste. Le 21:13-15; Eze 44:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-3","title":"2 Corinthians 11:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I fear. 29; 12:20,21; Ps 119:53; Ga 1:6; 3:1; 4:11; Php 3:18,19 as. Ge 3:4,13; Joh 8:44; 1Ti 2:14; Re 12:9; 20:2 so. 13-15; 2:17; 4:2; Mt 24:24; Ac 20:30,31; Ga 1:6; 2:4; 3:1; Eph 4:14 Eph 6:24; Col 2:4,8,18; 2Th 2:3-11; 1Ti 1:3; 4:1-4; 2Ti 3:1-9,13 2Ti 4:3,4; Tit 1:10; Heb 13:9; 2Pe 2:1-14; 3:3,17; 1Jo 2:18; 4:1 Jude 1:4; Re 12:9 the simplicity. 1:12; Ro 12:8; 16:18,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-4","title":"2 Corinthians 11:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>preacheth. Ac 4:12; 1Ti 2:5 receive. 1Co 12:4-11; Ga 3:2; Eph 4:4,5 another gospel. Ga 1:7,8 with him. or, with me.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-5","title":"2 Corinthians 11:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>I was not. 12:11,12; 1Co 15:10; Ga 2:6-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-6","title":"2 Corinthians 11:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>rude. 10:10; 1Co 1:17,21; 2:1-3,13 not. Eph 3:4; 2Pe 3:15,16 but we. 4:2; 5:11; 7:2; 12:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-7","title":"2 Corinthians 11:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>in. 10:1; 12:13; Ac 18:1-3; 20:34; 1Co 4:10-12; 9:6,12,14-18; 1Th 2:9 2Th 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-8","title":"2 Corinthians 11:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>9; Php 4:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-9","title":"2 Corinthians 11:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>wanted. 6:4; 9:12; Php 2:25; 4:11-14; Heb 11:37 I was. 12:13; Ne 5:15; Ac 18:3; 20:33; 1Th 2:9; 2Th 3:8,9 the brethren. 8:1,2; Php 4:10,15,16 See on ver. 8 burdensome. 12:14-16; 1Th 2:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-10","title":"2 Corinthians 11:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the truth. 31; 1:23; 12:19; Ro 1:9; 9:1; Ga 1:20; 1Th 2:5,10; 1Ti 2:7 no man shall stop me of this boasting. Gr. this boastingshall not be stopped in me. 12,16,17; 10:15; 1Co 9:15-18 the regions. 1:1; 9:2; Ac 18:12,27; Ro 16:5; 1Co 16:15; 1Th 1:7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-11","title":"2 Corinthians 11:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>because. 6:11,12; 7:3; 12:15 God. 10; 12:2,3; Jos 22:22; Ps 44:21; Joh 2:24,25; 21:17; Ac 15:8 Heb 4:13; Re 2:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-12","title":"2 Corinthians 11:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>what. 9; 1:17; Job 23:13 that I may. 1Co 9:12; 1Ti 5:14 them. Ga 1:7; Php 1:15-30 they glory. 18; 5:12; 10:17; 1Co 5:6; Ga 6:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-13","title":"2 Corinthians 11:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>false. 15; 2:17; 4:2; Mt 25:24; Ac 15:1,24; 20:30; Ro 16:18; Ga 1:7; 2:4; 4:17 Ga 6:12; Eph 4:14; Php 1:15,16; Col 2:4,8; 1Ti 1:4-7; 4:1-3; 6:3-5 2Ti 2:17-19; 3:5-9; 4:3,4; 2Pe 2:1-3; 1Jo 2:18; 4:1; 2Jo 1:7-11; Jude 1:4 Re 2:2,9,20; 19:20 deceitful. Php 3:2; Tit 1:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-14","title":"2 Corinthians 11:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>for. 3; 2:11; Ge 3:1-5; Mt 4:1-10; Ga 1:8; Re 12:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-15","title":"2 Corinthians 11:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>no. 2Ki 5:13; 1Co 9:11 his. 13; Ac 13:10; Eph 6:12; Re 9:11; 13:2,14; 19:19-21; 20:2,3,7-10 the ministers. 23; 3:9 whose. Isa 9:14,15; Jer 5:31; 23:14,15; 28:15-17; 29:32; Eze 13:10-15,22 Mt 7:15,16; Ga 1:8,9; Php 3:19; 2Th 2:8-12; 2Pe 2:3,13-22 Jude 1:4,10-13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-16","title":"2 Corinthians 11:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>say. 1 Let. 21-23; 12:6,11 receive me. or, suffer me. 1,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-17","title":"2 Corinthians 11:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>I speak it. 1Co 7:6,12 foolishly. 18-27; 9:4; Php 3:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-18","title":"2 Corinthians 11:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>many. 12,21-23; 10:12-18; Jer 9:23,24; 1Co 4:10; 1Pe 1:24 I will. 12:5,6,9,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-19","title":"2 Corinthians 11:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>seeing. 1Co 4:10; 8:1; 10:15; Re 3:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-20","title":"2 Corinthians 11:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>if a man bring. 1:24; Ga 2:4; 4:3,9,25; 5:1,10; 6:12 take. Ro 16:17,18; Php 3:19; 1Th 2:5 a man smite. Isa 50:6; La 3:30; Lu 6:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-21","title":"2 Corinthians 11:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>as though. 10:1,2,10; 13:10 whereinsoever. 22-27; Php 3:3-6 I speak. 17,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-22","title":"2 Corinthians 11:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Hebrews. Ex 3:18; 5:3; 7:16; 9:1,13; 10:3; Ac 22:3; Ro 11:1; Php 3:5 the seed. Ge 17:8,9; 2Ch 20:7; Mt 3:9; Joh 8:33-39; Ro 4:13-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-23","title":"2 Corinthians 11:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>ministers. 3:6; 6:4; 1Co 3:5; 4:1; 1Th 3:2; 1Ti 4:6 I am. 5; 12:11,12 in labours. 1Co 15:10; Col 1:29 in stripes. 24,25; 6:4,5; Ac 9:16 in prison. Ac 9:16; 16:24; 20:23; 21:11; 24:26,27; 25:14; 27:1; 28:16,30; Eph 3:1 Eph 4:1; 6:20; Php 1:13; 2Ti 1:8,16; 2:9; Phm 1:9; Heb 10:34 in deaths. 1:9,10; 4:11; 6:9; Ac 14:19; 1Co 15:30-32; Php 2:17; Col 1:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-24","title":"2 Corinthians 11:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>forty. De 25:2,3; Mt 10:17; Mr 13:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-25","title":"2 Corinthians 11:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>I beaten. Ac 16:22,23,33,37; 22:24 once. Mt 21:35; Ac 7:58,59; 14:5,19; Heb 11:37 thrice. Ac 27:1-44</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-26","title":"2 Corinthians 11:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>journeyings. Ac 9:23,26-30; 11:25,26; 13:1-14:28; 15:2-4,40,41; 16:1-18:1 Ac 18:18-23; 19:1; 20:1-6; Ro 15:19,24-28; Ga 1:17-21 in perils by mine. Ac 9:23-25,29; 13:50; 20:3,19; 21:28-31; 23:12-22; 25:3; 28:10,11 1Th 2:15,16 in perils by the. 1:8-10; Ac 14:5,19; 16:19-24; 19:23-41; 1Co 15:32 in perils in the city. 32; Ac 9:24; 17:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-27","title":"2 Corinthians 11:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>weariness. 23; 6:5; Ac 20:5-11,34,35; 1Th 2:9; 2Th 3:8 in watchings. Ac 20:31 in hunger. Jer 38:9; 1Co 4:11,12; Php 4:12 fastings. 6:5; Ac 13:2,3; 14:23; 1Co 7:5 nakedness. Ro 8:35,36; Heb 11:37; Jas 2:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-28","title":"2 Corinthians 11:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>those. 23-27 the care. Ac 15:36,40,41; 18:23; 20:2,18-35; Ro 1:14; 11:13; 15:16; 16:4 Col 2:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-29","title":"2 Corinthians 11:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>is weak. 2:4,5; 7:5,6; 13:9; Ezr 9:1-3; Ro 12:15; 15:1; 1Co 8:13; 9:22; 12:26 Ga 6:2; 1Th 3:5-8 and I burn. 13-15; Nu 25:6-11; Ne 5:6-13; 13:15-20,23-25; Joh 2:17; 1Co 5:1-5 1Co 6:5-7,15-18; 11:22; 15:12-34,36; Ga 1:7-10; 2:4-6,14; 3:1-3 Ga 4:8-20; 5:2-4; 2Jo 1:10,11; Jude 1:3,4; Re 2:2,20; 3:15-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-30","title":"2 Corinthians 11:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>must. 16-18; 12:1,11; Pr 25:27; 27:2; Jer 9:23,24 I will. 12:5-10; Col 1:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-31","title":"2 Corinthians 11:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>God. 1:3,23; Joh 10:30; 20:17; Ro 1:9; 9:1; Eph 1:3; 3:14; Ga 1:2,3 Col 1:3; 1Th 2:5; 1Pe 1:3 which. Ne 9:5; Ps 41:13; Ro 1:25; 9:5; 1Ti 1:11,17; 6:16 knoweth. 10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-32","title":"2 Corinthians 11:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>Damascus. 26; Ac 9:24,25 Aretas.This Aretas was an Arabian king, and the father-in-law of Herod Antipas, upon whom he made war in consequence of his having divorced his daughter. Herod applied to Tiberius for help, who sent Vitellius to reduce Aretas, and to bring him alive or dead to Rome. By some means or other Vitellius delayed his operations, and in the mean time Tiberius died; and it is probable that Aretas, who was thus snatched from ruin, availed himself of the favourable state of things, and seized on Damascus, which had belonged to his ancestors.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-2co-11-33","title":"2 Corinthians 11:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"2CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>I let. Jos 2:18; 1Sa 19:12</p>"}]}